ial_on_rn_e979973d_012","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"For $f(x,y) = 3x^2y^4$, which statement correctly describes $f(\\lambda x,\\lambda y)$?","options":["$f(\\lambda x,\\lambda y) = \\lambda^6 f(x,y)$","$f(\\lambda x,\\lambda y) = \\lambda^2 f(x,y)$","$f(\\lambda x,\\lambda y) = \\lambda^4 f(x,y)$","$f(\\lambda x,\\lambda y) = 6\\lambda f(x,y)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"746678080780a1b8110b2ec9"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_monomial_on_rn_85bde1a2_013","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Is the expression $x^2+y$ a monomial on $\\mathbb{R}^2$?","options":["No; a monomial is a single product term, not a sum","Yes; every polynomial is a monomial","Yes; any combination of powers is a monomial","Only when the two exponents are equal"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1968e0670b6a48875a2d0b48"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_monomial_on_rn_85bde1a2_014","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What is the total degree of the constant monomial $f(x,y)=5$?","options":["$0$","$5$","$1$","It has no total degree"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5e73176266f6ed5879926d1c"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_monomial_on_rn_85bde1a2_015","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"When two monomials are multiplied, what happens to their coefficients?","options":["They are multiplied together","They are added","They are kept as a list","They are reset to $1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6b78193d2cf4ecef691f88cf"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_monomial_on_rn_85bde1a2_016","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is the total degree of $-3x^2y^4$?","options":["$6$","$4$","$2$","$-3$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"670ea41b6089dc96044169b0"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_monomial_on_rn_85bde1a2_017","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which expression is NOT a monomial on $\\mathbb{R}^2$?","options":["$x+y$","$3x^2y$","$5y^4$","$x^2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7ee46a3fe2a16c5976517b54"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_monomial_on_rn_85bde1a2_018","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is the coefficient of the product $(2x^2y)(3xy^4)$?","options":["$6$","$5$","$8$","$1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"365d027c5d646452c52bb31f"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_monomial_on_rn_85bde1a2_019","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"The product of two monomials on $\\mathbb{R}^n$ is always:","options":["another monomial","a sum of two monomials","a polynomial of degree $2$","undefined"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"13090ebafe4a858c5ac5506a"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_monomial_on_rn_85bde1a2_020","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $f(x,y)=x^3y$, how does $f(2x,2y)$ compare with $f(x,y)$?","options":["$f(2x,2y)=16\\,f(x,y)$","$f(2x,2y)=8\\,f(x,y)$","$f(2x,2y)=4\\,f(x,y)$","$f(2x,2y)=2\\,f(x,y)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4b6a67538c1b36fd173ed7ba"}]}}